om":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T02:12:44-08:00","id":429960,"title":"","content":"I would have thought the Gentry and goblins would be the trainers. The thought of that makes me feel sorry for the changelings. Pokehell <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T10:50:41-08:00","id":430414,"title":"","content":"I assumed most changelings would be forced into the pok\u00e9mon role. Changeling trainers would be very few.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T18:32:24-08:00","id":432097,"title":"","content":"Hu, then may I propose a question. How would the pokeball work and what if it could work outside the hedge?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T21:37:21-08:00","id":432240,"title":"","content":"Definitely Tokens. Probably not functional outside of Arcadia. But I think a given ball would take a Composure vs. Wyrd roll to capture a target, and only hold one particular changeling or hob (as long as that one's alive, anyway). If they work on Earth... euch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T07:55:17-07:00","id":435698,"title":"","content":"Like the idea !!! Oh yeah, a real life pikachu in the WoD, su much epicness !<br /> <br /> For the pokeball, a token creating instantly a hedge portal leading to an inescapable cell ? With some mecanics like what Ladylens said ? <br /> <br /> For the trainers there is in i-didn't-remember-which book (rites of spring i think, but not so sure) a merit for taming Hobgoblin. It's will be easy to make it a kith, for Fairest (child trainer) or Ogre (classical slave trainer).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3883-arabidopsis","name":"Arabidopsis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T01:59:12-07:00","id":439624,"title":"","content":"This... this is...why does this have so much potential? The Twisted ver. of pokemon WOD /Changeling style? Changelings that are enslaved by their TrueFae/trainers. Forced to fight and capture their comrades. Newbie/low levels that go into the hedge get picked off the fastest, unless they learn to stay ahead of the chase to get stronger or face there captors. Wryld/leveling up. Staying in motleys to survive. Including a lot of in-fighting and betrayal. a pikachu, paralyzes his ally ,just so they can use them as a bargaining chip to be let go, or getting a pass out of the hedge. Definitely seeing a lot of Drama via &quot;Lord of the Flies&quot; &quot;Predator&quot; and &quot;Surviving the Game&quot; elements.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>&quot;I am a daydreamer and a Night thinker.&quot;~</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1820-nightout","name":"Nightout","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T21:46:32-07:00","id":450126,"title":"","content":"Hmmm I'll have to present this idea to my group and let them use the hedge-balls in the normal world. Who will win? Mage or werewolf? Took in next week folks... Ya a good idea to let the chaos out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T21:59:30-07:00","id":450133,"title":"","content":"While looking into this idea thanks to you guys, well hedgespun items can do the truck. Changelings need a recipe and materials. Goblin fruit just became the pokemon version of berries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T06:38:23-07:00","id":454178,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\">While I can see Trainers being Loyalists, I doubt the Gentry would approve of mere mortals having authority over their play things. So yeah, I can imagine trainers being Gentry constantly on the hunt for new pokemon, and making them battle each other for glory, fame, and wealth.<br /> <br /> There are 719 species of Pokemon right now... that's <b>a lot</b> of slaves!<br /> <br /> <br /> This makes even more sense with the release of the new &quot;Fairy&quot; type Pokemon. :P<br /> <br /> And then, of course, we have The Daycare... where trainers force their pokemon to breed!<br /> <br /> <br /> Motley's could be translated into a Swarm battle.<br /> <br /> <br /> If the Changelings are lucky, they'll meet a Trainer who's attempting the Nuzlocke challenge!</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-23-2015, 10:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T06:55:53-07:00","id":454196,"title":"","content":"After giving it some thought, I feel like the Seemings would appropriately fit the following types of pokemon.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> Any type available. Commonly Dual Kith<br /> <br /> <b>Elementals:</b> Fire, Grass, Electric, Steel, Ground, Water, Rock<br /> <br /> <b>Darkling:</b> Poison, Dark, Ghost<br /> <br /> <b>Fairest:</b> Dragon, Fairy, Psychic, Flying<br /> <br /> <b>Ogre:</b> Fighting, Bug<br /> <br /> <b>Wizened:</b> Fighting, Normal","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T07:16:09-07:00","id":454332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/426867-gotta-catch-em-all?p=454178#post454178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And then, of course, we have The Daycare... where trainers force their pokemon to breed!</div> </div> </div> </div>And we all know how successful that will be. Also, what's the Nuzlocke challenge?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T09:26:50-07:00","id":454466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/426867-gotta-catch-em-all?p=454332#post454332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And we all know how successful that will be. Also, what's the Nuzlocke challenge?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The Nuzlocke Challenge was created for hard core Pokemon players. The rules are very simple, but they make the game extremely difficult.<br /> <br /> Rule 1 - NO REVIVES, EVER. If a pokemon faints in battle, you must release it back into the wild.<br /> <br /> Rule 2 - The first pokemon you encounter in a new area is the only one you're allowed to catch from there.<br /> <br /> <br /> One of the more popular Nuzlocke challenges has Nuptup, Destroyer of Worlds. She's a vileploom who devours the souls of her victims with drain attacks. She fainted in battle, but the game immediately crashed, and when the Let's Player started it back up again, she was alive once more. Thus leading to theories that Nuptup can not be killed by mortal means.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xdN0G4rBHAI\" target=\"_blank\">Rise of Nuptup</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-23-2015, 12:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T09:31:20-07:00","id":454473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/426867-gotta-catch-em-all?p=454332#post454332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And we all know how successful that will be. Also, what's the Nuzlocke challenge?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Nuzlocke_Challenge\" target=\"_blank\">Here ya go.</a> Basically, a self-imposed challenge, with rules to make the game more difficult. The particular bit Nyrufa's likely referring to is that a Pokemon who faints is released. I'm not so sure that's how it'd work for the Changeling, though: the rule technically is that a Pokemon who faints <i>is considered dead</i>, and release is just the in-game simulation thereof. Also, there seem to be alternative rules involving permanently boxing, migrating, or transferring fainted Pokemon, which might not be too fun, either.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, a trainer who has nothing but fainted Pokemon is handed a game over. A Gentry who's metaphysically tied itself to that and a savvy Changeling team that's figured out the rules could bludgeon themselves unconscious, destroying their Keeper and securing their freedom thereby.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T10:10:35-07:00","id":454532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/426867-gotta-catch-em-all?p=454473#post454473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, a trainer who has nothing but fainted Pokemon is handed a game over. A Gentry who's metaphysically tied itself to that and a savvy Changeling team that's figured out the rules could bludgeon themselves unconscious, destroying their Keeper and securing their freedom thereby.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the <i>other</i> other hand, the arcane rules of turn-based combat and the established capacity for the Others to prevent their charges from dying or passing out could force a more complicated resolution.<br /> <br /> I'm ill-equipped to explain why, but somehow this is making me think of &quot;jobbers&quot; in professional wrestling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T10:54:21-07:00","id":454603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/426867-gotta-catch-em-all?p=454532#post454532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the <i>other</i> other hand, the arcane rules of turn-based combat and the established capacity for the Others to prevent their charges from dying or passing out could force a more complicated resolution.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also quite true. Even if it could in principle work out as I described, there's also the idea that the Strangers might have decided that &quot;fainted&quot; in the Pokemon games was describing <i>actual death</i>. In which case, the team of Changelings could do great harm to their Keeper, but only by committing collective suicide. So, uh. Hard sell and pyrrhic victory, there.<br /> <br /> I'm wondering why I framed that as a definite in my post, given my tendency most of the time to go the other way. Ah well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm ill-equipped to explain why, but somehow this is making me think of &quot;jobbers&quot; in professional wrestling. </div> </div> </div>Not well-acquainted with wrestling, though I think I've encountered the term. On an unrelated note, this conversational tangent makes me think of the South Park episode where all the little league teams are trying to lose to one another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T15:55:32-07:00","id":454965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/426867-gotta-catch-em-all?p=454532#post454532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the <i>other</i> other hand, the arcane rules of turn-based combat and the established capacity for the Others to prevent their charges from dying or passing out could force a more complicated resolution.<br /> <br /> I'm ill-equipped to explain why, but somehow this is making me think of &quot;jobbers&quot; in professional wrestling.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Well these are the Fae, we're talking about. Their whole society is based on rules, so maybe they'd play by our terms.<br /> <br /> <br /> Crap, now I really want to see a Changeling Pokemon series! <b>Hope this pic shows up</b>. :P</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://d.facdn.net/art/carlito/1266904567/1266904567.carlito_audryessmash.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T05:19:16-07:00","id":455700,"title":"","content":"Come to think of it, early generations of pokemon wouldn't be so bad in the Changeling world...<br /> <br /> and then we have shit like <a href=\"http://www.serebii.net/pokedex-xy/568.shtml\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Trubbish</b></a> and <a href=\"http://www.serebii.net/pokedex-xy/583.shtml\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Vanillish</b></a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T05:42:13-07:00","id":456758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/426867-gotta-catch-em-all?p=455700#post455700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Come to think of it, early generations of pokemon wouldn't be so bad in the Changeling world...<br /> <br /> and then we have shit like <a href=\"http://www.serebii.net/pokedex-xy/568.shtml\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Trubbish</b></a> and <a href=\"http://www.serebii.net/pokedex-xy/583.shtml\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Vanillish</b></a></div> </div> </div> </div>Ach, you wound my trubbish-loving little heart. I honestly think a gross, trash-bag-themed Blightbent with a jagged overbite would be a rather unfortunate AND humorous character to play.<br /> <br /> In all seriousness, though, I love this whole thread and concept a lot!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>i don't know a hecking thing, my guy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4416-heedra","name":"Heedra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T08:20:40-07:00","id":456886,"title":"","content":"Please, Grimer is much more adorable than a torn trash bag! Looks a lot happier with his life too!<br /> <br /> Ohh... then we have a Cubone changeling... holy crap...<br /> <br /> BTW: Did the pic show up above us? I wasn't sure if that site allowed its pics being linked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-25-2015, 11:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T08:33:44-07:00","id":456892,"title":"","content":"I admit, I didn't really think Grimer looked all that happy, until I observed what its face looks like slapped onto other Pokemon. Like <a href=\"http://pokemon.alexonsager.net/88/123\" target=\"_blank\">Scyther</a>, <a href=\"http://pokemon.alexonsager.net/88/139\" target=\"_blank\">Omastar</a>, or <a href=\"http://pokemon.alexonsager.net/88/151\" target=\"_blank\">Mew</a>.<br /> <br /> On a related topic, Pokemon Fusion would probably also be a horrible addition to this playspace.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T08:50:21-07:00","id":456905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/426867-gotta-catch-em-all?p=456892#post456892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I admit, I didn't really think Grimer looked all that happy, until I observed what its face looks like slapped onto other Pokemon. Like <a href=\"http://pokemon.alexonsager.net/88/123\" target=\"_blank\">Scyther</a>, <a href=\"http://pokemon.alexonsager.net/88/139\" target=\"_blank\">Omastar</a>, or <a href=\"http://pokemon.alexonsager.net/88/151\" target=\"_blank\">Mew</a>.<br /> <br /> On a related topic, Pokemon Fusion would probably also be a horrible addition to this playspace.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I know I said the first gen pokemon wouldn't be so bad, but now that I think about it, a heck of a lot of pokemon, you probably don't want to be turned into. Imagine the poor Changeling who gets turned into Electrode. Their existence spent as a living explosive that can go off at random.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"htt