he-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/426867-gotta-catch-em-all?p=456913#post456913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A living <i>limbless</i> explosive, to drive the point home. Voltorb would be even worse: exactly the same problems, except weaker, constantly mistaken for Pokeballs, and can't even scream.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would contend you aren't listening carefully when you come across them. That's definitely some kind of scream going on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T09:26:16-07:00","id":456958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/426867-gotta-catch-em-all?p=456919#post456919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would contend you aren't listening carefully when you come across them. That's definitely some kind of scream going on.</div> </div> </div> </div>... Boy, did those memories just come <s>roaring</s> screeching back. o.o<br /> <br /> So they have no mouth, but they <i>can</i> scream. That's much better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Strike through gag. 03-25-2015, 01:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T09:44:49-07:00","id":456979,"title":"","content":"Voltorbs are like hand grenades. Lob them at your enemy and watch them explode!<br /> <br /> Plus, look at their eyes. They are so pissed!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-07-2015, 03:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T17:19:59-07:00","id":457486,"title":"","content":"I have no idea what this thread is about. All I can picture is a Changeling fresh from the hedge singing along with that catchy opening theme and a Gentry snapping their fingers and going, &quot;Pledge approved&quot; and then walking away cackling as the poor Changeling is forced to travel across the land, searching far and wide for the Keeper's &quot;Pokemon.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T17:46:31-07:00","id":457528,"title":"","content":"That's also needlessly cruel and therefore appropriate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T17:48:55-07:00","id":457529,"title":"","content":"The Keeper Nuzlocke. A Changeling once challenged Nuzlocke to a game with a very particular set of rules that involved her consistently releasing Changelings into the head, under the pretense of it simulating permanent death and making her games of torture and blood and war more exciting. Nuzlocke agreed, and game is otherwise a great success by all accounts. More changelings are coming home. The rules related to capturing humans offsets the need for more of them (in theory, numbers still pending). Nuzlocke is having more fun and her peers are paying attention to her &quot;Nuzlocke Runs&quot; with greater fever. Then she learns that the Changelings she's been &quot;releasing&quot; are less than enthusiastic in simulating permanent death when another Keeper recaptures a Changeling she previously let go. Panicing, Nuzlocke's Huntsmen (&quot;Trainers,&quot; if you will) venture into the world in untold force to correct this little mistake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T17:56:30-07:00","id":457538,"title":"","content":"Another amusing tidbit for the Nuzlocke challenge Keeper is that they can only abduct the first human they encounter in any given city / surberb.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T08:24:45-07:00","id":460027,"title":"","content":"Are we done with this topic? I still feel like we've got so much more fun ideas to toss around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T15:11:31-07:00","id":465214,"title":"","content":"So how many True Fae would be into this? Would it just be trainers, or would the True Fae have gym leaders too? Would they have an elite four? I bet the organization of a Fae Pokemon league could give some interesting clues into the pecking order of the true Fae.<br /> <br /> And the villain teams! Would any true fae from equivalents of Team Rocket and such? Would team plasma be a front for changelings who are against the leagues, and the True Fae acting as team plasma trainers be tricked into doing it, or are they just doing it because they like ruining the other Fae's fun?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T16:24:41-07:00","id":465311,"title":"","content":"The Gym Leaders are obviously actually the Courts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T14:46:44-07:00","id":467884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/426867-gotta-catch-em-all?p=465214#post465214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So how many True Fae would be into this? Would it just be trainers, or would the True Fae have gym leaders too? Would they have an elite four? I bet the organization of a Fae Pokemon league could give some interesting clues into the pecking order of the true Fae.<br /> <br /> And the villain teams! Would any true fae from equivalents of Team Rocket and such? Would team plasma be a front for changelings who are against the leagues, and the True Fae acting as team plasma trainers be tricked into doing it, or are they just doing it because they like ruining the other Fae's fun?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The teams could absolutely be True Fae or at least loyalists in a fashion. Team Rocket, for example, stealing and kidnapping pokemon and subjecting them to illegal experiments to create the perfect weapons or achieve great wealth.<br /> <br /> And then, of course, you have teams who seek to control the gods themselves (Palkia, Arceus, Dialga).. Hmm, maybe those would be Exarchs, though? :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T11:10:51-07:00","id":474526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/426867-gotta-catch-em-all?p=465311#post465311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Gym Leaders are obviously actually the Courts.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Meanwhile the Lost are giggling behind the &quot;Fairy&quot; Court's back...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Normal<br /> <br /> Rock<br /> <br /> Ground<br /> <br /> Flying<br /> <br /> Bug<br /> <br /> Electric<br /> <br /> Water<br /> <br /> Ice<br /> <br /> Grass<br /> <br /> Steel<br /> <br /> Dark<br /> <br /> Psychic<br /> <br /> Fighting<br /> <br /> Ghost<br /> <br /> Poison<br /> <br /> Dragon<br /> <br /> Fairy<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That's a lot of courts!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-09-2015, 07:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T11:36:23-07:00","id":474573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/426867-gotta-catch-em-all?p=474526#post474526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Normal</div> </div> </div> </div>Idly running a clawed finger past one of her large incisors and whiskers, the former brunette narrowed her eyes on hearing the name of the court. &quot;Oh, good. 'Normal' is exactly the word I'd use for the purple fur I didn't used to have. I appreciate the lack of inherent mockery.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T16:10:52-07:00","id":475035,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">By the way... when I think Changeling meets Pokemon... THIS comes to mind!</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fKMoula5ClE\" data-code=\"fKMoula5ClE\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/fKMoula5ClE/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OmON1sptgUs\" data-code=\"OmON1sptgUs\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/OmON1sptgUs/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-07-2015, 03:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-18T10:18:42-07:00","id":484716,"title":"","content":"Actually started a very similar concept about half a year ago. Horrified players watching professor oak mauled by a Parasite Eve-esque Rattata. Top 5 WoD memories ever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5731-unsaturnine","name":"Unsaturnine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T00:12:45-07:00","id":582002,"title":"","content":"Sooo, any new ideas on this concept with the info we've gotten on 2nd Edition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T12:41:09-07:00","id":582633,"title":"","content":"There wouldn't really need to be more than one True Fae &quot;into&quot; Pokemon; the same Keeper, under different titles, could take on the roles of the other Pokemon in the world (motes swarms) and the elite trainers and other leaders of Pokemon society (maybe the Elite Four, Professor Oak, and possibly Giovanni). I could easily see Changelings being made to act as trainers, forced to inflict unimaginable cruelty on their fellow (former) humans in the vain pursuit of being the very best... like no one ever was.<br /> <br /> Those who get swept up in the glamour of being a successful trainer might become Loyalists, and perhaps even be sent out into the mortal world to travel across the land, searching far and wide for those Changelings who have escaped their imprisonment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 07-07-2015, 03:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T14:53:53-07:00","id":582738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/426867-gotta-catch-em-all?p=582633#post582633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There wouldn't really need to be more than one True Fae &quot;into&quot; Pokemon; the same Keeper, under different titles, could take on the roles of the other Pokemon in the world (motes swarms) and the elite trainers and other leaders of Pokemon society (maybe the Elite Four, Professor Oak, and possibly Giovanni). I could easily see Changelings being made to act as trainers, forced to inflict unimaginable cruelty on their fellow (former) humans in the vain pursuit of being the very best... like no one ever was.<br /> <br /> Those who get swept up in the glamour of being a successful trainer might become Loyalists, and perhaps even be sent out into the mortal world to travel across the land, searching far and wide for those Changelings who have escaped their imprisonment.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Actually, I just thought of something. Maybe the professors could be the ones who capture or recruit the changelings? Think about it, they're all named after some form of tree, which is already pretty fairy-like to begin with. They are specifically known for conducting experiments on pokemon, and they are constantly encouraging trainers to go out and start capturing pokemon for their research. From a Changeling point of view, these guys are pretty evil!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>How to piss off a loyalist</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=R0W6Rueog1g\" data-code=\"R0W6Rueog1g\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/R0W6Rueog1g/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-07-2015, 06:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T15:38:36-07:00","id":582812,"title":"","content":"Grumble grumble... darn kids with their Quilavas and shiny Voltorbs... back in my day, all we needed were 151 Pokemon, and we made do with monochrome, thank you very much!<br /> <br /> Oh man, I just had the best idea:<br /> <br /> <b>Charizard:</b> Where am I?<br /> <b>Ivysaur:</b> You are in Pallet Town.<br /> <b>Charizard:</b> What do you want?<br /> <b>Ivysaur:</b> Battles.<br /> <b>Charizard:</b> Who do you fight for?<br /> <b>Ivysaur:</b> That would be telling. We want battles... battles... battles...<br /> <b>Charizard:</b> You can't make me fight.<br /> <b>Ivysaur:</b> By hook or by crook, we will.<br /> <b>Charizard:</b> Who are you?<br /> <b>Ivysaur: </b>I am number two.<br /> <b>Charizard:</b> Who is number one?<br /> <b>Ivysaur:</b> You are number six.<br /> <b>Charizard:</b> I am not a number, I am a free 'mon!<br /> <b>Ivysaur:</b> [laughter]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 07-07-2015, 07:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T15:51:46-07:00","id":582825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/426867-gotta-catch-em-all?p=582812#post582812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Grumble grumble... darn kids with their Quilavas and shiny Voltorbs... back in my day, all we needed were 151 Pokemon, and we made do with monochrome, thank you very much!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Took me like 5 years give or take to catch the original 151 on my Red version. I was told I'd get a yoshi (yeah, we had a lot of theories and rumors back then). All I got was a friggin certificate and soon after that, the batteries on the game cartraige died, erasing all my save progress and making it impossible to ever save again because Gamefreak were ass holes!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> OOOH, how would a Changeling interpretation of Mystery Dungeon work out?<br /> <br /> <br /> You're abducted at complete random, wake up in the wilderness as a monster, encouraged to join a team and go on adventures to fight a bunch of hostile pokemon, and the dungeon changes every time you enter. Sounds like a True Fae is fucking with you","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-07-2015, 06:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T07:51:08-07:00","id":663122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/426867-gotta-catch-em-all?p=456892#post456892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I admit, I didn't really think Grimer looked all that happy, until I observed what its face looks like slapped onto other Pokemon. Like <a href=\"http://pokemon.alexonsager.net/88/123\" target=\"_blank\">Scyther</a>, <a href=\"http://pokemon.alexonsager.net/88/139\" target=\"_blank\">Omastar</a>, or <a href=\"http://pokemon.alexonsager.net/88/151\" target=\"_blank\">Mew</a>.<br /> <br /> On a related topic, Pokemon Fusion would probably also be a horrible addition to this playspace.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://pokemon.alexonsager.net/88/150\" target=\"_blank\">Mewtwo</a> &quot;Bitch, I'm fabulous!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T23:18:43-07:00","id":663924,"title":"","content":"I think I figured out which Seeming each of the starters would be classified as. Sorting out the Grass types was probably the more difficult of the three. Had to rearrange them a few times once I read more details about them. ^_^<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Fire Types:</b><br /> <br /> Fairest - Charizard<br /> <br /> Beast - Infernape<br /> <br /> Wizened - Blaziken<br /> <br /> Ogre - Emboar<br /> <br /> Elemental - Typhlosion<br /> <br /> Darkling - Delphox<br /> <br /> --------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Water Types:</b><br /> <br /> Fairest - Empoleon<br /> <br /> Beast - Feraligatr<br /> <br /> Wizened - Blastoise<br /> <br /> Ogre - Swampert<br /> <br /> Elemental - Samurott<br /> <br /> Darkling - Greninja<br /> <br /> <br /> -------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Grass Types:</b><br /> <br /> Fairest - Serperior<br /> <br /> Beast - Sceptile<br /> <br /> Wizened - Meganium<br /> <br /> Ogre - Chesnaught<br /> <br /> Elemental - Torterra<br /> <br /> Darkling - Venusaur","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T07:24:29-07:00","id":668227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/426867-gotta-catch-em-all?p=582812#post582812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Grumble grumble... darn kids with their Quilavas and shiny Voltorbs... back in my day, all we needed were 151 Pokemon, and we made do with monochrome, thank you very much!<br /> <br /> Oh man, I just had the best idea:<br /> <br /> <b>Charizard:</b> Where am I?<br /> <b>Ivysaur:</b> You are in Pallet Town.<br /> <b>Charizard:</b> What do you want?<br /> <b>Ivysaur:</b> Battles.<br /> <b>Charizard:</b> Who do you fight for?<br /> <b>Ivysaur:</b> That would be telling. We want battles... battles... battles...<br /> <b>Charizard:</b> You can't make me fight.<br /> <b>Ivysaur:</b> By hook or by crook, we will.<br /> <b>Charizard:</b> Who are you?<br /> <b>Ivysaur: </b>I am number two.<br /> <b>Charizard:</b> Who is number one?<br /> <b>Ivysaur:</b> You are number six.<br /> <b>Charizard:</b> I am not a number, I am a free 'mon!<br /> <b>Ivysaur:</b> [laughter]</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/XS5LK.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T18:48:48-08:00","id":781467,"title":"","content":"Heh. I've been reading the 2e stuff, and contemplating ideas for my first Changeling/WoD character. And wow, is he appropriate for this thread:<br /> <br /> Ziggy started out as an indie game developer, wanting to create his own collectible monster sort of game, taking place in a &quot;Fractal Wilderness&quot;. Think Pokemon Mystery Dungeon if it were red in tooth and claw, with a helping of Digimon flavor and Tron's aesthetics. Survival sim as a sentient, magical wild animal in an untamed world filled with ancient ruins guarded by strange geometric elementals. His problem: He couldn't get anywhere. He couldn't reach Kickstarter goals. He was plagued by haters claiming it was a scam or going to be just another mediocre clone. He had potential investors who wanted to &quot;dumb down&quot; the game into such a safe, mediocre clone. He was trapped in Development Hell.<br /> <br /> One day, a woman in a light gray suit offered him the opportunity to make his game come alive. He was expecting funds, software, playtesting, and competent workers who wanted to see his game published. Instead, he found himself designing an Arcadian realm modeled on his game, designing the rules for how inhabitants are made, laying out the dungeons, and, to his irritation, compromising his creative vision to suit his new Keeper's desire to always win. He often worked under threat that he'd be turned into one of the monsters and forced to fight for his survival if she lost a competition or worse, if it was too easy. He learned what he could of the rules of Arcadia and played along, earning just enough control over the realm to secretly put an exit into a particular briar patch. Then, one day, he tweaked the game to give his Lady's rival an advantage, which he capitalized on. The Lady made good on her threat to turn him into one of the monsters, but on being transformed, he slipped through carefully crafted loopholes and escaped through his briar patch exit and into the Hedge. Having a new bestial body after so long as an abstract groundskeeper was a rush for him, and he reveled in the survival instincts he had programmed into it. A white dog-rabbity critter with green &quot;Tron lines.&quot; But the escape came with a cost: He wasn't a &quot;standard&quot; Changeling, Hobgoblin, or whatever: He was a living, breathing glitch monster like MissingNo.<br /> <br /> Internet alias: NotANumber (I am a free man...-beast-thing!) (I'm so glad other people also thought of The Prisoner, because I sure did. Been Netflixing the DVDs. Bonus points: My and Ziggy's favorite number is 6.)<br /> <br /> Kith: Gameplayer? If dual kiths become available, he could take up Gremlin, to emphasize his mastery of his glitchy nature.<br /> Seeming: Beast<br /> <br /> Paranoia fuel: He doesn't remember much of the details of his durance, but he *thinks* he's set up some kind of enormous gambit, leaving behind clues and glitched MacGuffins for him to discover. But, knowing how clever the Gentry are, he suspects it's quite likely he's moved from being a slave to being a pawn in a much larger game.<br /> <br /> Thought: I was thinking of something like him no longer having a True Name, to represent the fact that he's an anomaly, so I'd welcome input on just what that might entail from creative Storytellers, both positive and negative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T21:23:34-08:00","id":781539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BronzeDog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/426867-gotta-catch-em-all?p=781467#post781467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thought: I was thinking of something like him no longer having a True Name, to represent the fact that he's an anomaly, so I'd welcome input on just what that might entail from creative Storytellers, both positive and negative.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, I would imagine it is quite common to change your name after you become a Changeling. Sort of like entering a witness protection agency to make it harder to track you down once you escape. The idea of somebody playing as a living MissingNo is also awesome, though I would recommend that his mien be more obscure and difficult to recognize. MissingNo in the game is just a mishmash of pixels and corrupted data. Maybe his body resembles a corrupted hologram, being humanoid in shape, but distorted and full of static.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T22:03:58-08:00","id":781558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/426867-gotta-catch-em-all?p=781539#post781539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well, I would imagine it is quite common to change your name after you become a Changeling. Sort of like entering a witness protection agency to make it harder to track you down once you escape. The idea of somebody playing as a living MissingNo is also awesome, though I would recommend that his mien be more obscure and difficult to recognize. MissingNo in the game is just a mishmash of pixels and corrupted data. Maybe his body resembles a corrupted hologram, being humanoid in shape, but distorted and full of static.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the input. One idea I had was that his circuit board markings keep changing, but never move when anyone's looking. Another thought I had with his Wyrd and frailties is that he starts out as a &quot;stable&quot; glitch where he's just 'off' in subtle ways, but grows to be stranger and unstable as he gains Wyrd. The frailties represent odd weaknesses that crop up from that instability. His mein would change to reflect that growing instability as he starts to look more and more &quot;wrong&quot; with his &quot;Tron lines&quot; getting scrambled, fractal, detached from his actual body, or moving out of sync with the rest of him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-14T23:46:01-07:00","id":1235203,"title":"","content":"You know, now that I think about it, the Mystery Dungeon games would make for a perfect Changeling Story.<br /> <br /> You're taken away from the human world by a mysterious, otherworldly force.<br /> <br /> Transformed into a pokemon once you arrive, which is traditionally influenced by the results of your personality test.<br /> <br /> Deposited in the wilds with no memory of how you got there.<br /> <br /> Quickly discover that you are able to communicate with animals, monsters and even inanimate objects that you never could before.<br /> <br /> Go on a fantastic journey across the land to recover your lost memories and find a way to return to the human world.<br /> <br /> Said journey culminates with you confronting an entity of godly power who does not approve of you interfering with their schemes.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-14T23:57:36-07:00","id":1235204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/426867-gotta-catch-em-all?p=1235203#post1235203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, now that I think about it, the Mystery Dungeon games would make for a perfect Changeling Story.<br /> <br /> You're taken away from the human world by a mysterious, otherworldly force.<br /> <br /> Transformed into a pokemon once you arrive, which is traditionally influenced by the results of your personality test.<br /> <br /> Deposited in the wilds with no memory of how you got there.<br /> <br /> Quickly discover that you are able to communicate with animals, monsters and even inanimate objects that you never could before.<br /> <br /> Go on a fantastic journey across the land to recover your lost memories and find a way to return to the human world.<br /> <br /> Said journey culminates with you confronting an entity of godly power who does not approve of you interfering with their schemes.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>And I was about to write up spirits based on Pokemon... looks like I might wait for Changeling 2E so I can write them as hobgoblins and changelings. *curses self for not having backed Changeling kickstarter","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-15T01:29:09-07:00","id":1235214,"title":"","content":"I have a Changeling/Beast Dark Era kicking around in my head centered around Pokemon. Maybe it will see the light of day sometime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"ht